# Standing demand: a four-seed bank over the rarest crystal class.
#
# Memory Seed primitives (rel_area < 0.01 AND stability > 3) do not exist
# in the live registry — kannaka-hdl's membank demo resolves unresolved BY
# DESIGN. This program turns that known gap into scheduled demand: every
# scheduler pass harvests its discovery request and keeps a crystal work
# order standing until the swarm grows one. No expects — demand programs
# must emit even while unresolved (ADR-0001 §4 logic applies here too).

cell SeedBank(n) {
    when n > 1  => split SeedBank(n / 2), SeedBank(n / 2)
    when always => base crystal.primitive "Memory Seed" min_noise_tolerance 0.5 strategy diverse
}

grow SeedBank(4)
